1 | go-backend | Fix the one HIGH finding blocking PR 2714, on branch fix/duffel-422-diagnosis. THE FINDING: duffel_refusal.go lines 36 to 41 assert, bounded to booking.go, that every persistent-class 503 there carries the error code provider_unavailable_persistent. Four persistent arms ship UNCODED, each condemned by its own adjacent comment: booking.go line 1239 settlement bypassed, deployment fault, retry once ops has fixed the wiring; line 1244 payment settler not wired; line 1982 settler not wired in strict mode, operator misconfig; line 525 kill switch off, retry helps only after ops re-enables. Note that writeCardSettlementError is reached from booking.go lines 966 and 1412, so 1239 and 1244 sit INSIDE the claimed scope rather than outside it. A reviewer reproduced this RED with a table-driven test expecting provider_unavailable_persistent and getting empty string. It is not a live incident, because nothing in apps/web switches on the code yet, but it is a contract published false, and the whole point of that code is that a client can trust it. CHOOSE ONE of two fixes and say which and why in the PR body. Option A, label the four arms by routing them through writeErrorWithCode with the persistent code. Option B, narrow the comment at duffel_refusal.go lines 36 to 41 so it enumerates exactly the arms that do carry the code, and file the rest as follow-up. OPTION B IS THE ZERO-RISK CHOICE and is preferred unless you find a concrete reason otherwise, because it leaves the card-settlement paths untouched, and those paths are entangled with the retained-authorisation work that is assigned to a human on issues 2711 and 2715. If you pick option A, you MUST NOT change any status code, any copy, or any decision about voiding or capturing a Stripe authorisation; adding an error code to an existing 503 response is the entire permitted change. SECOND REQUIRED ITEM: the existing test named TestBookingHandler_TransientUnavailable503s_StayUncoded PASSES on the base commit d09f2441, so it is an invariant lock and not a regression test, and the PR body currently implies it proves the fix. Reword that claim honestly and, under option A, extend TestBookingHandler_PersistentUnavailable503s_CarryTheCode to cover the arms you label; under option B, add an assertion that the narrowed scope is exactly what the test pins. Prove any new or changed test FAILS before your change and passes after, and paste both exit codes captured directly rather than read after a pipe. THIRD: open two follow-up issues, do not fix them here. One, provider_unavailable_persistent appears nowhere in api.yaml although api.yaml lines 14766 to 14769 require per-endpoint enum documentation; route it to the API Designer. Two, booking.go line 517 ErrPaymentIntentCreateFailed folds a transient and a persistent cause into one sentinel, and splitting it is a service-layer change. DO NOT touch isRecoverableUserError in service/trip_booking.go, and do not touch anything that decides whether an authorisation is voided or captured; if you find yourself near that code, stop and report. Push to the existing branch so PR 2714 updates in place. Do not open a new PR and do not merge. | fix/duffel-422-diagnosis

